{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607031800-kami-genre-base-systems"
  :title "ADR-2607031800: kami-genre-base-systems -- 18 genre-category base gameplay systems for kotoba-lang"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kami-genre-base-systems"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-03"
  :authoritative_for
  ["kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems holds base/foundation gameplay
    systems, one per genre category from a PlayStation-Store-style
    genre-browse taxonomy (generic genre LABELS only, never any specific
    commercial title's characters/art/story/mechanics)"
   "18 categories were requested; not all are gameplay-mechanic archetypes
    -- 4 (modern-remake/free-to-play/indie/post-apocalyptic) are
    business/production/setting categories with no distinct core loop of
    their own, and this repo does not force-invent a fake mechanic to claim
    18/18 identical-shape 'real systems' -- each of those 4 instead gets a
    real, honestly-labelled SUPPORTING SYSTEM a game in that category would
    plausibly need (a tuning-preset layer, a currency/economy loop, a
    minimal starter kernel, a resource-scarcity system), not a claim that
    the category itself is a mechanic"
   "all 18 categories now have real, clojure -M author.clj-verified
    author.clj+logic.clj pairs, built strictly within the kami-clj compiler
    subset's proven vocabulary (cross-checked against every reference game
    this session established: kami-clj-play/games/{survivors,waves},
    kami-clj-play3d/games/{royale,rt-audio-demo,dance})"
   "local-multiplayer and fighting both use the same honest '1 human + 1
    AI' adaptation isekai-network's own concept-3 investigation established
    as the only currently-buildable local-multiplayer shape, given the
    confirmed single-local-input-stream engine constraint"
   "a maturity pass added 1-3 additional defsystems/richer state per
    category (scoped honestly, not padded for parity) deepening each
    genre's core loop beyond its bare minimal proving mechanic"]
  :related
  ["CLAUDE.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607023200-isekai-network-standalone-repo.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607031700-kotoba-lang-engine-wasm-emission-and-host-runtime.md"
   "gftdcojp/isekai-network (the precedent this repo's author.clj/logic.clj
    shape and honesty discipline follows)"
   "kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []}

 :problem
 {:source "user request: pasted a PlayStation Store genre-browse page
            (real commercial titles as genre examples), asked for just the
            category labels extracted, then asked for a base gameplay
            system per category 'as kotoba-lang'"
  :investigated
  ["the pasted list mixed two things: real commercial game titles/key-art
    descriptions (copyrighted, must not be reproduced/mimicked) and generic
    genre category labels (not copyrightable, safe to use as organizing
    labels for wholly original systems) -- the category-label-only
    extraction the user explicitly requested resolved this cleanly before
    any system-building began"
   "the kami-clj compiler subset's proven vocabulary, established
    cumulatively across this whole session's isekai-network work, is
    genuinely constrained: single local input stream (no player-index axis
    argument anywhere), no terrain/tilemap/pathfinding/vehicle-physics/
    skeletal-animation reachable from guest logic (Rust-substrate only),
    no multiplication operator confirmed anywhere in any reference game or
    prior verified base system (checked before use, not assumed) -- every
    system in this repo was built to fit inside these real constraints,
    not an idealized unconstrained design"
   "4 of the 18 requested categories are not gameplay archetypes at all --
    forcing them into the same 'distinct core loop' shape as the other 14
    would have meant fabricating fictional mechanics with no grounding,
    the same failure mode this session's design-investigation work (concept
    2-5 open-questions) repeatedly rejected for isekai-network itself"]
  :risk "18 base systems is a large surface -- risk of quality dilution
         (shallow, near-identical copies) or risk of dishonest padding on
         the 4 non-mechanic categories to hit a round number. Both were
         explicitly guarded against: real per-genre design distinctions
         (see :decision below), and honest N/A/preset framing for the 4
         business/setting categories rather than fabricated mechanics"}

 :decision
 {:repo {:path "kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems"
         :visibility :public
         :structure "design/<genre>.edn (one design doc per category,
                     schema: :genre/id :genre/core-loop :genre/controls
                     :genre/kami-engine{:proven-vocab-used :known-constraints})
                     + games/<genre>/{author.clj,logic.clj,deps.edn,.gitignore}
                     (one pair per category with real code) -- mirrors
                     kami-clj-play/games/'s established convention exactly"}
  :fourteen_gameplay_archetypes
  ["rhythm (beat-gated tick-n+mod timing, the pattern isekai-network's own
     concept 1/4 proved and this repo's rhythm system directly reuses) --
     maturity pass added a defatom combo/streak counter"
   "puzzle -- maturity pass added a second distinct tile-arrangement
     variant so there is real progression, not one static puzzle"
   "stealth -- maturity pass replaced binary detected/not-detected with an
     escalating defatom alert-level that rises on detection and decays over
     time"
   "single-player (the canonical survivors-shaped reference loop plus a
     defatom level counter escalating spawn tightness)"
   "strategy -- maturity pass added a real win/lose condition (opposing
     defatom force counters, game ends at zero)"
   "sports (ball-and-goal proximity mechanic)"
   "horror (escalating pursuit-speed tension loop)"
   "superhero (empowered/wide-range combat, themed reskin of the base
     weapon system)"
   "open-world (large flat arena + scattered point-of-interest discovery,
     honestly NOT streaming terrain -- that fidelity is Rust-substrate
     only)"
   "local-multiplayer (1 human + 1 AI vs a shared ball/objective, honest
     fallback for the confirmed single-input-stream constraint)"
   "kids-family (deliberately the simplest base in the repo -- zero-fail
     stationary-collection loop, no chase AI at all)"
   "relaxing (player-paced 'garden' touch-to-grow loop, no timer pressure)"
   "platformer (sequential ordered-waypoint traversal -- honestly NOT a
     jump-physics platformer; no jump/gravity primitive exists anywhere in
     the proven vocabulary, confirmed via a targeted grep across every
     reference game before concluding this)"
   "fighting (1 human + 1 AI opponent, same input-stream constraint as
     local-multiplayer, proximity-exchange defatom health counters)"]
  :four_supporting_systems_not_mechanics
  ["modern-remake -- a real, reusable TUNING-PRESET system (wider hit-
     tolerance, auto-aim-style larger weapon-range) demonstrated by
     re-tuning single-player's constants, not a fabricated 'remake
     mechanic'"
   "free-to-play -- a real soft-currency economy loop (earn via enemy
     defeat, auto-spend at a threshold for a temporary buff, buff decays)
     layered on single-player -- a genuine common F2P building block, not a
     claim that F2P is itself a mechanic"
   "indie -- the smallest possible starter kernel in the repo (one entity,
     one movement system, nothing else) -- a genuinely useful rapid-
     iteration starting point, explicitly labelled as a scaffold not a
     genre mechanic"
   "post-apocalyptic -- a real resource-scarcity system (limited weapon
     defatom 'charges' depleting per use, replenished by scarce 'salvage'
     pickups) layered on single-player -- a genuine scarcity mechanic, not
     a claim that the narrative setting is inherently a distinct core loop"]
  :verification
  "every author.clj actually run via `clojure -M author.clj`, confirmed
   producing valid scene.edn; every logic.clj construct cross-checked
   against the proven vocabulary (defsystem/defn/def/let/when/cond/if/f32/
   spawn-entity/despawn-entity/set-position!/set-velocity!/get-x/get-y/
   nearest-tagged/count-tagged/doseq-entities/move-toward!/axis/tick-n/mod/
   rand-int/zero?/</=/not=/defatom/set-atom!) -- multiplication was checked
   and found NOT confirmed anywhere in any reference game or prior verified
   base, so score-reset-style periods use precomputed constants with a
   comment explaining the derivation, rather than an unverified `*` call.
   WASM compilation (kotoba-lang/engine's compile-file) was NOT attempted
   for all 18 in this pass -- a legitimate, valuable follow-up, out of
   scope here given this session's established slow-build cost for that
   verification tier"}

 :consequences
 {:reusable_foundation "18 genre-labelled starting points now exist for any
                         future kotoba-lang game project to fork from,
                         each with documented, honestly-scoped engine
                         constraints rather than aspirational unverified
                         claims"
  :discipline_precedent "the honest N/A-vs-real-mechanic distinction
                          methodology (4/18 categories) is now a concrete,
                          citable precedent for any future taxonomy-driven
                          content generation task in this org -- 'hit every
                          requested slot' does not override 'do not
                          fabricate'"
  :follow_up_debt "WASM-compile verification for all 18 games remains
                    undone; a natural next pass once genuinely needed by a
                    real consuming game project, not speculative work now"}

 :alternatives
 [{:option "force all 18 categories into an identical 'distinct core loop'
            shape, inventing mechanics for the 4 business/setting
            categories"
   :rejected_because "would have fabricated ungrounded gameplay claims for
                       categories that are not gameplay archetypes -- the
                       same failure mode this session's isekai-network
                       design-investigation work (concept 2-5) repeatedly
                       and deliberately avoided"}
  {:option "skip the 4 non-mechanic categories entirely (no games/ dir,
            no code at all)"
   :rejected_because "the user explicitly asked for real code for these 4
                       too -- the honest resolution was a real, clearly-
                       labelled supporting system per category, not silence"}
  {:option "attempt real hecs/pathfinding/physics integration for genres
            that traditionally need it (strategy pathfinding, platformer
            physics, sports vehicles) instead of the gameplay-logic-only
            approximation"
   :rejected_because "these are Rust-substrate crates unreachable from
                       kami-clj guest logic -- confirmed, not assumed, via
                       this session's repeated concept-level investigations
                       for isekai-network. Attempting it here would have
                       required new host-side engine work out of scope for
                       a base-systems content repo"}]}
